WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
How's everybody
doing tonight?

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.705 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Wally's kid, you good?

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
Alright.
Can we get you anything?

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.376 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[Indistinct]

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.944 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Alright. Alright.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:12.479 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Let's get to the news.

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:14.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
President Biden
met with Senate Democrats

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the White House yesterday
and committed to boosting

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
coronavirus relief checks
to $2,000.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:23.723
But don't forget, you alread
got a $1,200 one and a $600 one,

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
plus the standard
20% inflation,

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.794 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
makes it $2,180.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, basically,
you owe $180.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.299
President Biden spoke at
the State Department today

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:36.302 size:88% position:44%
and gave his first major
foreign policy speech.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:40.073 size:84% position:42%
Of course, these days,
any speech about policy

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:40.740 size:78% position:39% line:92%
feels pretty foreign.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
"When's he gonna talk abou
water pressure?

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:45.945 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Is that not in today's?"

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
House Republicans,
last night,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
held a five-hour
conference meeting.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, to have been a fly
on literally any other wall.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
During last night's House
Republican conference meeting,

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:00.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
GOP members gave
QAnon-supporting congresswoman

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:03.163 size:81% position:41%
Marjorie Taylor Greene
a standing ovation --

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:04.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
though, based on
what I know about her,

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:08.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
the smarter move
is to get down.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
House Minority Leader
Kevin McCarthy, yesterday,

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:14.741
referred to the conspiracy
theory group QAnon as "Qon,"

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said, quote,
"I don't even know what it is.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:21.981
Added McCarthy, "Maybe I can ask
Donald Trank? Trimp?

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.383 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Is it Tramp?

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that how you say it?
I'll ask him."

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's right --
Kevin McCarthy, yesterday,

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:30.523
referred to the conspiracy group
QAnon as "Qon,"

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said, quote,
"I don't even know what it is.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:36.696
Ah, the time-tested strategy
of mispronouncing somethin

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
on purpose
to distance yourself.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like a kid
who got caught with weed.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, this? This is my...
my friend Dave's.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess it's marywonka,
or something.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:50.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's a spice
from home ec."

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
Former Housing
and Urban Development secretar

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:56.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dr. Ben Carson announced
yesterday that he is launching

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
a conservative
think tank.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:59.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
It'll be dedicated
to examining

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:02.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
the pertinent problems
of our time,

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.289 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and trying to find...

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.858 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-My luggage.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:10.296
-Netflix, yesterday, receive
42 Golden Globe nominations.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when you're working on
your speeches,

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.334 size:81% position:41% line:92%
you know who to thank.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:17.337
And finally, the makers of Peeps
have announced

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
they'll release
two new flavors --

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hot Tamales
and Froot Loops.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you think
that's gross,

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:26.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
wait till you see
what you release.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:29.282 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Baze!

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.084 size:78% position:39% line:92%
That was a monologue.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:31.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
There he is.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:34.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
BGaze and Wally's kid,
just living it up.

